From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 21:42:11 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: usb: dwc2: Add usb-psy-name

Some boards charge from the USB device port through a charger that has no
usb_phy and so cannot learn through usb_phy_set_power() what the host
allows the device to draw. The snps,dwc3 driver solves the same problem by
naming the power supply in usb-psy-name. Document the same property for
dwc2.

J71t ledger 6.8 (gadget current reported through vbus_draw).

Signed-off-by: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/dwc2.yaml | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/dwc2.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/dwc2.yaml
index 166d37cd9..b1f66a663 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/dwc2.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/usb/dwc2.yaml
@@ -172,6 +172,13 @@ properties:
     description: If present indicates that we need to reset the PHY when we
       detect a wakeup. This is due to a hardware errata.
 
+  usb-psy-name:
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/string
+    description:
+      Name of the power supply that limits the input current drawn from the
+      USB port. In gadget mode it is told the current the host allows the
+      device to draw, as the snps,dwc3 controllers do with the same property.
+
   port:
     description:
       Any connector to the data bus of this controller should be modelled
